free cloud compute?

Eventually the economic optimizer isn't a “model router.”

It's a resource router.

Also, QDW's own operating rules already insist that missing economic data must not silently become zero and that work is only proven through recorded verification. That is extremely compatible with WorkerKit.

I didn't find a literal indexed HotRouter symbol in the current qdw tree during this pass, so I wouldn't anchor an API contract to that exact name yet. But the QDW/Forge/Sandbox resource abstractions are clearly the right layer to reuse.
The subtle point: don't simply “use free compute first”

Instead:

    Maximize useful value extracted from expiring free compute.

Free compute still has an opportunity cost.

Suppose you have:

10,000 Cloudflare neurons left

Task A:
classification
almost any model works

Task B:
medium-quality code review
free GLM happens to be quite good

Task C:
difficult architectural reasoning
strong model vastly better

If you burn the whole free quota on A at noon, you may have to pay for B at night.

So assign every quota bucket a shadow price.

Conceptually:

effective_cost(model, task)
 =
money_cost
+
quota_shadow_cost
+
latency_cost
+
expected_retry_cost
+
failure_risk

For a free model:

money_cost = 0

but:

quota_shadow_cost != 0

while that quota is scarce.

Then something interesting happens near reset:

10 hours until reset
quota remaining: 90%
      ↓
shadow price falls

30 minutes until reset
quota remaining: 70%
      ↓
shadow price ≈ 0

At that point the Lab should become aggressive:

unused free compute?
        ↓
pull useful jobs from backlog
        ↓
run evaluations
re-grade trajectories
generate candidates
test weak-model routing
summarize research
build indexes
generate synthetic exercises
mine failure patterns

Not because “we need to use the quota,” but because the marginal cost has effectively gone to zero.

That is a really interesting scheduler.
